{
 "capitulo": 16,
 "titulo_en": "You must wear a helmet",
 "titulo_es": {
  "@es": "Obligaciones, prohibiciones y reglas",
  "@en": "Obligations, prohibitions and rules"
 },
 "palabras": {
  "must": {
   "es": "deber (obligación)",
   "pron": "mast"
  },
  "mustn't": {
   "es": "no debes; no se puede",
   "pron": "MÁ-sent",
   "consejo": {
    "@es": "Prohibición.",
    "@en": "Prohibition."
   }
  },
  "helmet": {
   "es": "casco",
   "pron": "JÉL-met"
  },
  "seat belt": {
   "es": "cinturón de seguridad",
   "pron": "SÍT-belt"
  },
  "rule": {
   "es": "regla",
   "pron": "rul"
  },
  "allowed": {
   "es": "permitido; permitida",
   "pron": "a-LÁUD"
  },
  "smoke": {
   "es": "fumar",
   "pron": "smóuk"
  },
  "warn": {
   "es": "advertir; avisar",
   "pron": "uorn",
   "consejo": {
    "@es": "No significa «aconsejar»; eso es «advise».",
    "@en": "It doesn't mean «aconsejar»; that's «advise»."
   }
  },
  "sleep": {
   "es": "dormir",
   "pron": "slip"
  }
 },
 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Must: obligación",
    "@en": "Moss: obligation"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**Must** + verbo base expresa una obligación fuerte, a menudo una regla: **You must wear a helmet** (debes llevar casco). No cambia con la persona: **I must**, **she must**.",
     "@en": "**Must** + base verb expresses a strong obligation, often a rule: **You must wear a helmet** (you must wear helmet). It does not change with the person: **I must**, **she must**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Puede sonar como una orden. Una **rule** indica lo que es obligatorio o está prohibido.",
     "@en": "It may sound like an order. A **rule** indicates what is mandatory or prohibited."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Mustn't: prohibido",
    "@en": "Mustn-o: prohibited"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**Mustn't** = no debes, no se puede: **You mustn't smoke here** (no puedes fumar aquí). Es una prohibición.",
     "@en": "**Mustn't** = you should not, you cannot: **You mustn't smoke here** (you cannot smoke here). It's a ban."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Ojo: **mustn't** no es «no tienes que». Eso es **don't have to**, y lo vemos en la lección siguiente.",
     "@en": "Eye: **mustn't** is not «You don't have to.». That's **don't have to**, and we see it in the next lesson."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Distingue warn de advise",
    "@en": "Distinguish warn de notice"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**Warn** = advertir o avisar de un peligro. **Advise** = aconsejar. No son intercambiables: **I must warn you** = debo advertirte.",
     "@en": "**Warn** = warning or warning of a danger. **Advise** = advise. They are not interchangeable: **I must warn you** = I must warn you."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "vocabulario",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Vocabulario: reglas",
    "@en": "Vocabulary: rules"
   },
   "palabras": [
    "must",
    "mustn't",
    "helmet",
    "seat belt",
    "rule",
    "allowed",
    "smoke",
    "warn",
    "sleep"
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "dialogo",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Reglas de seguridad vial",
    "@en": "Road safety rules"
   },
   "frases": [
    {
     "quien": "Liz",
     "en": "We must wear a helmet when we ride our bikes.",
     "es": "Debemos llevar casco cuando vamos en bicicleta.",
     "analisis": [
      [
       "must wear",
       {
        "@es": "debemos llevar",
        "@en": "We must take"
       }
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "quien": "Pedro",
     "en": "And in the car, we must wear a seat belt.",
     "es": "Y en el coche debemos llevar cinturón de seguridad.",
     "analisis": [
      [
       "must wear",
       {
        "@es": "debemos llevar",
        "@en": "We must take"
       }
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "quien": "Liz",
     "en": "Drivers mustn't drive after drinking alcohol.",
     "es": "Los conductores no deben conducir después de beber alcohol.",
     "analisis": [
      [
       "mustn't drive",
       {
        "@es": "no deben conducir",
        "@en": "you should not drive"
       }
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "quien": "Pedro",
     "en": "That's right. They mustn't smoke in the car, either.",
     "es": "Así es. Tampoco deben fumar en el coche.",
     "analisis": [
      [
       "mustn't smoke",
       {
        "@es": "no deben fumar",
        "@en": "do not smoke"
       }
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "quien": "Liz",
     "en": "I don't drink alcohol or smoke.",
     "es": "No bebo alcohol ni fumo.",
     "analisis": [
      [
       "don't drink",
       {
        "@es": "no bebo",
        "@en": "I don't drink."
       }
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "quien": "Pedro",
     "en": "Good. You must get enough sleep before a long drive.",
     "es": "Bien. Debes dormir lo suficiente antes de un viaje largo.",
     "analisis": [
      [
       "must get enough sleep",
       {
        "@es": "debes dormir lo suficiente",
        "@en": "You must sleep long enough."
       }
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "test",
   "pregunta": {
    "@es": "¿Qué expresa «mustn't» en «You mustn't smoke here»?",
    "@en": "What does «mustn't» express in «You mustn't smoke here»?"
   },
   "id": "en124-1",
   "opciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Una prohibición: no debes fumar aquí.",
     "explicacion": {
      "@es": "**Mustn't** expresa que algo está prohibido.",
      "@en": "**Mustn't** states that something is forbidden."
     },
     "correcta": true
    },
    {
     "texto": "No tienes que fumar aquí.",
     "explicacion": {
      "@es": "Eso sería «don't have to».",
      "@en": "That would be «don't have to»."
     }
    },
    {
     "texto": "Puedes fumar aquí.",
     "explicacion": {
      "@es": "Eso expresa permiso; **mustn't** lo prohíbe.",
      "@en": "That expresses permission; **mustn't** forbids it."
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "test",
   "pregunta": {
    "@es": "¿Qué forma va en «You ___ wear a helmet»?",
    "@en": "What's the way in «You ___ wear a helmet»?"
   },
   "id": "en124-2",
   "opciones": [
    {
     "texto": "must",
     "explicacion": {
      "@es": "Obligación fuerte: must + verbo base.",
      "@en": "Strong obligation: must + verb base."
     },
     "correcta": true
    },
    {
     "texto": "must to",
     "explicacion": {
      "@es": "Con must no va «to».",
      "@en": "With must not go «to»."
     }
    },
    {
     "texto": "musts",
     "explicacion": {
      "@es": "Must no cambia.",
      "@en": "Moss doesn't change."
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "traduccion",
   "pregunta": {
    "@es": "¿Qué significa?",
    "@en": "What does that mean?"
   },
   "frase": "¿Qué expresa «must» en «You must sleep»?",
   "id": "en124-3",
   "opciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Una obligación: debes dormir.",
     "explicacion": {
      "@es": "**Must** expresa aquí una obligación.",
      "@en": "**Must** expresses an obligation here."
     },
     "correcta": true
    },
    {
     "texto": "Una costumbre: duermes todos los días.",
     "explicacion": {
      "@es": "Eso describe una rutina.",
      "@en": "That describes a routine."
     }
    },
    {
     "texto": "Un permiso: puedes dormir.",
     "explicacion": {
      "@es": "Eso expresa permiso, no obligación.",
      "@en": "That expresses permission, not obligation."
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "huecos",
   "pregunta": {
    "@es": "No debes",
